             polled in client mode, a ‘^’ indicates that the server is broad‐
             casting to this address, a ‘~’ denotes that the remote peer is
             sending broadcasts and a ‘~’ denotes that the remote peer is
             sending broadcasts and a ‘*’ marks the peer the server is cur‐
             rently synchronizing to.

             The contents of the host field may be one of four forms.  It may
             be a host name, an IP address, a reference clock implementation
             name with its parameter or RREEFFCCLLKK(_i_m_p_l_e_m_e_n_t_a_t_i_o_n___n_u_m_b_e_r,
