             These commands operate in the same way as the eennaabbllee and ddiissaabbllee
             configuration file commands of ntpd(8).

             aauutthh    Enables the server to synchronize with unconfigured peers
                     only if the peer has been correctly authenticated using
                     either public key or private key cryptography.  The de‐
                     fault for this flag is enable.

             bbcclliieenntt
                     Enables the server to listen for a message from a broad‐
                     cast or multicast server, as in the multicastclient com‐
                     mand with default address.  The default for this flag is
                     disable.

             ccaalliibbrraattee
                     Enables the calibrate feature for reference clocks.  The
                     default for this flag is disable.

             kkeerrnneell  Enables the kernel time discipline, if available.  The
                     default for this flag is enable if support is available,
                     otherwise disable.

             mmoonniittoorr
                     Enables the monitoring facility.  See the documentation
                     here about the mmoonnlliisstt command or further information.
                     The default for this flag is enable.

             nnttpp     Enables time and frequency discipline.  In effect, this
                     switch opens and closes the feedback loop, which is use‐
                     ful for testing.  The default for this flag is enable.

             ppppss     Enables the pulse-per-second (PPS) signal when frequency
                     and time is disciplined by the precision time kernel mod‐
                     ifications.  See the "A Kernel Model for Precision
                     Timekeeping" (available as part of the HTML documentation
                     provided in _/_u_s_r_/_s_h_a_r_e_/_d_o_c_/_n_t_p) page for further informa‐
                     tion.  The default for this flag is disable.

             ssttaattss   Enables the statistics facility.  See the _M_o_n_i_t_o_r_i_n_g
                     _O_p_t_i_o_n_s section of ntp.conf(5) for further information.
                     The default for this flag is disable.

